later; see the LICENSE file at the root of the repository.

2. Permitted use without a subscription

You may copy, modify and run the Software, free of charge, only to:
  a. develop, test and debug LibreHR or the Software itself;
  b. contribute changes back to the LibreHR project;
  c. evaluate the Software in a non-production environment for up to
     30 days.
"Production" means any use with real employee data or for real business
operations.

3. Production use

Production use requires one of:
  a. a valid LibreHR licence key covering the features and the number of
     employees in use, issued by the Licensor; or
  b. a LibreHR Cloud subscription; or
  c. a separate written agreement with the Licensor (for example a partner
     agreement).
The licence ends automatically when the key or subscription expires. After
that, Business features stop working but the Community edition and all of
your data remain available to you.

4. Restrictions

Unless a written agreement with the Licensor says otherwise, you may not:
